Which equation represents the absolute value graph shown below?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.0]
\draw[->] (-1.5,0) -- (6.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-1) -- (0,7.5) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \x in {-1,1,2,3,4,5,6} {\draw (\x,0.1) -- (\x,-0.1); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.1) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y in {2,4,6} {\draw (0.1,\y) -- (-0.1,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.1,\y) {$\y$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[thick, <->] (-0.5,7) -- (3,0) -- (6,6);
\fill (3,0) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (0,6) circle (2pt);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Which equation represents the absolute value graph shown below?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.0]
\draw[->] (-4.5,0) -- (2.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-1) -- (0,6) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \x in {-4,-3,-2,-1,1,2} {\draw (\x,0.1) -- (\x,-0.1); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.1) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y in {1,2,3,4,5} {\draw (0.1,\y) -- (-0.1,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.1,\y) {$\y$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[thick, <->] (-4,4) -- (-2,0) -- (0.8,5.6);
\fill (-2,0) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (0,4) circle (2pt);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
